WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.680
Emryhs Cooper, Actor/Filmmaker: I didn't&nbsp;
really have a secure place to live.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:03.440 --> 00:00:08.160
I lived in about eight different homes and at one&nbsp;
point I actually became homeless and I lived in my&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:08.160 --> 00:00:15.920
car off Mulholland. So that was really a lot and I&nbsp;
was quite proud, so I didn't want to tell anyone.

00:00:15.920 --> 00:00:21.760
Film Courage: Skipping forward to 2008,&nbsp;
why were you confident that you could&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.320 --> 00:00:29.960
become an actor, come to Los Angeles, and&nbsp;
be in this crazy town full of crazy people?

00:00:29.960 --> 00:00:33.840
Emryhs: I'm quite a fearless&nbsp;
kind of person and I always just&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:34.400 --> 00:00:41.520
gamble on myself I guess. I left home when&nbsp;
I was 16 to pursue the arts. I left England&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:41.520 --> 00:00:48.160
to come to LA at 23. I watched a documentary about&nbsp;
Hollywood in the studio system in the 40's when I&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:48.160 --> 00:00:54.080
was about 13 years old and I just thought it&nbsp;
looked really magical (storytelling). I had&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:54.080 --> 00:01:01.520
quite a rough upbringing being bullied and just&nbsp;
a lot of kind of it was hard you know. I think I&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:01.520 --> 00:01:07.520
had this life outside of the dark situation in&nbsp;
movies that was my escape and I just kind of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:07.520 --> 00:01:13.120
thought of Hollywood as just a magical land and&nbsp;
it really is. I mean there's obviously all the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:13.120 --> 00:01:17.760
stereotypes about LA exist but I just wanted to&nbsp;
experience it and I've never been to America.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:18.400 --> 00:01:24.400
I saved up money from my last musical theater job&nbsp;
and got on the plane. I actually forgot my wallet&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:24.400 --> 00:01:30.800
which was so stupid so I arrived in LA with no&nbsp;
wallet and my phone didn't work and this lady&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:30.800 --> 00:01:35.440
who I actually never met came to pick me up and&nbsp;
I didn't have a phone it was a bit of a nightmare&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:35.440 --> 00:01:41.920
so it was a bit of a rocky start let's say but I'm&nbsp;
kind of grateful for all the challenges because it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:41.920 --> 00:01:48.720
made me have perseverance and staying power and it&nbsp;
makes me appreciate where I am now having a happy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:48.720 --> 00:01:54.000
home life and having a good circle of friends I&nbsp;
had to start from scratch when I was 23 and that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:54.000 --> 00:01:58.400
was kind of you know it was challenging but it&nbsp;
was good to push myself out of the comfort zone&nbsp;&nbsp;

